(SETTLEMENT SPECIFICATION v2.3) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Scope) Tj T*
(This document defines how an authorized payment becomes a ledger entry.) Tj T*
(It covers capture, webhook handling and correction rows.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. Capture) Tj T*
(A capture request may settle less than the authorized amount but never more.) Tj T*
(A capture above the authorized amount is rejected with 422.) Tj T*
(Authorization expires after 7 days; a capture after that returns 422.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. Idempotency) Tj T*
(Every settlement carries the payment idempotency key.) Tj T*
(The ledger enforces uniqueness on that key with a database constraint,) Tj T*
(not with an application-level check. See incident 2026-03-12.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
7 0 obj
<< /Length 635 >>
stream
BT
/F1 11 Tf
14 TL
56 740 Td
(4. Webhook handling) Tj T*
(The PSP retries webhooks until it receives a 2xx. Retries are expected) Tj T*
(and are not an error condition. The worker must be safe to run twice.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. Correction rows) Tj T*
(The ledger is append-only. A wrong entry is corrected by appending a row) Tj T*
(with the opposite sign, never by updating or deleting the original.) Tj T*
(The daily total must match after every correction batch.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6. Amounts) Tj T*
(All amounts are integers in the smallest currency unit.) Tj T*
(Floating point is not used anywhere in the settlement path.) Tj T*
ET
